 "equipment_type": "Power and energy meter",
 "applies_to": "Schneider Electric PowerLogic PM750 power meters on Modbus, read by a BASgatewayLX.",
 "summary": "Gateway profile for the PowerLogic PM750: 115 objects (99 AI, 1 AO, 15 BI), all polled. Inputs give energy totals, power totals and per phase, PF, voltages, currents, THD, present and peak demand, minimum/maximum values, usage time and the alarm status bits; one output writes reset commands.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Schneider_Power_Meter_750_LX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/SchneiderElectricPowerMeter750.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "All 115 rows are flagged for polling in the profile, so every object is served to BACnet once the profile is loaded.",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
  "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Voltage A-N THD Minimum; Voltage B-N THD Minimum; Voltage C-N THD Minimum...); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
 ],
 "source": {
